.radix 16

load_file (CS:13ad) move file by name to a buffer by pointer
vocab, demodata and wolf.chr each have their own special buffer
the rest are loaded to file_buffer (DS:2bd) size 3FF4
the biggest file loaded there is graphic file titlepix at 4000 bytes 
other files loaded there are the castle files at 3FF4 bytes: BACKUP CASTLE DEMOFILE SEKTOR. 
and the much smaller text-mode graphic files DEMOMESG and PRESSER
finally the graphic files ESCPIX1 and ESCPIX2 also at 4000 bytes are loaded to file buffer
    at 1 page offset.
so all in all the buffer has to have size of 4100. the graphics files either leave alone
    the first or last page, and the castle files take 40 pages but leave 0C bytes unused
    from their last page.
on that note draw_field0 (CS:503) draw to screen from the start of page 0,  
    the start of page 1, or from somewhere in page 0 of file_buffer. Or from the start of wolf.chr's buffer
main (CS:640) sets PTR_file_buffer (DS:46be) to point to file_buffer. This (2bd) is also the 
    value it is initialized to from the executable.  save_castle (CS:de8) also set it to 
    that value.
Both save_castle and Load_castle_page_w/_ptr (CS:da7) access file_buffer thru PTR_file_buffer
    (in save_castle case only after it sets it)
save_castle saves from file_buffer to file with a name it was given. 
    first it copy from castle page to page_0 of the file_buffer
    then it writes 3FF4 bytes from the beginning of file_buffer to the
    file it was given (between opening and closing off course)
save_castle is only called with castle and backup